> A hand-checkable calculation

With on-policy importance ratios1 and zero baseline Q/V, terminal rewards1,2 at discount.5 produce Retrace targets2,2. The experiment keeps bias correction, logit-gradient projection and average-policy synchronization explicit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/acer_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -lpthread -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");std::vector<float>rewards{1,2},done{0,1},mu{.5,.5,.5,.5},p{.5,.5,.5,.5,.5,.5},q{0,0,0,0,0,0},v{0,0,0};std::vector<int>a{0,0};auto target=dm::rl::off_policy::Retrace(rewards,done,a,mu,p,q,v,2,.5f);std::vector<double>values(target.begin(),target.end());std::print("| coordinate | computed value |\n|---:|---:|\n");for(size_t i=0;i<values.size();++i)std::print("| {} | {:.9f} |\n",i,values[i]);dm::nn::save_npz("build/acer_worked.npz",{{"values",dm::nn::from_vector(values)}});std::vector<double>x(values.size());std::iota(x.begin(),x.end(),0.);double low=std::min(0.,*std::min_element(values.begin(),values.end())),high=std::max(0.,*std::max_element(values.begin(),values.end())),span=std::max(1.,high-low);dm::graphics::RPlot::create().bars(x,values,"worked values",{37,99,235}).ylim(low-.05*span,high+.05*span).title("acer worked calculation").x_label("Displayed coordinate").size(1000,550).save_svg("build/acer_worked.svg");}
